<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battles of Khalkhin Gol</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1939">1939</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Nomonhan Incident · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-japanese-border-conflicts">Soviet–Japanese border conflicts</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battles of Khalkhin Gol, known in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> as the Nomonhan Incident, were fought from May to September 1939 on the Khalkhin Gol river on the border between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongolia">Mongolia</a> and Japanese-controlled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchukuo">Manchukuo</a>. Soviet and Mongolian forces under Georgy Zhukov encircled and destroyed much of the Japanese 23rd Division in August. The defeat turned Japan away from war with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>, and the two countries signed a neutrality pact in 1941.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battles-of-khalkhin-gol.jpg" alt="Battles of Khalkhin Gol" width="320" height="206" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dōmei Tsushin · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Japanese_soldiers_creeping_in_front_of_wrecked_Soviet_tanks.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…launched the invasion of the rest of China after the Marco Polo Bridge incident of 1937, and in May 1939 a clash between Manchukuoan and Mongolian cavalry grew into the <b>Battles of Khalkhin Gol</b>, in which a combined Soviet–Mongolian force defeated the Kwantung Army with limited Manchukuoan support.</blockquote><a href="/empire/manchukuo">Manchukuo · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Soviet and Mongolian forces defeated Japan at <b>Khalkhin Gol</b> in 1939.</blockquote><a href="/state/mongolian-peoples-republic">Mongolian People's Republic</a></li></ul></section>
